  "notes": "Weight matrix: rows = leg size a x a (mm), columns = wall thickness (mm), cells = theoretical weight kg/m; empty cell = size/thickness combination not listed. The label-column header is printed on two lines (\"Matmenys,\" / \"mm.\"). Thickness columns are not consecutive at the end: ... 18, 19, 20, 22, 24, 26, 28 (no 21, 23, 25, 27). Column placement was taken from the 22 vertical grid lines of the body (x = 93 + 43*k px); header labels sit at x = 96 + 43*k px and every body value starts exactly 3 px right of its cell's left border, so no value straddles two columns. Row 100x100, column 7 is printed with one decimal (\"10.7\") while all other cells have two decimals - kept as printed. Row 140x140: the cells for 11 and 12 mm are blank and covered by a white rectangle that also hides the grid lines there (looks like values erased in the source); 27.50 sits in column 13. From 10 kg/m upwards the values are printed as x.x0 except four cells that really are printed with a non-zero second decimal: 140x140/14 = 29.42, 160x160/10 = 24.58, 180x180/12 = 33.05, 200x200/14 = 42.69. White / light-blue row backgrounds are plain zebra striping; this image has no stock legend. Body text is a non-antialiased bitmap font: every glyph matched a digit template exactly (pixel-exact round trip JSON -> glyphs -> image: 0 mismatches in 552 cells, ink pixel totals identical); all bands re-read visually at 2x and 3x."
